  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. Partners secretly agree on a signal (gesture, word, or movement) to indicate they have four-of-a-kind\n2. Each player receives 4 cards\n3. Four cards are placed face-up in the center\n4. When play begins, players simultaneously exchange cards with the center\n5. Players can swap any number of cards (1-for-1, 2-for-2, etc.)\n6. No turns - it's a free-for-all\n7. Players try to collect four-of-a-kind in their hand\n8. When a player gets four-of-a-kind, they give their secret signal to their partner\n9. The partner calls 'Kemps!' to score a point\n10. If 'Kemps' is correct, the team scores\n11. If 'Kemps' is wrong (false alarm), the team loses a point\n12. Opponents can call 'Stop Kemps' or 'Counter-Kemps' if they think someone is signaling\n13. If a 'Stop Kemps' is correct, the calling team scores; if wrong, they lose a point",
    Player: "1. Partners secretly agree on a signal (gesture, word, or movement) to indicate they have four-of-a-kind\n2. Each player receives 4 cards\n3. Four cards are placed face-up in the center\n4. When play begins, players simultaneously exchange cards with the center\n5. Players can swap any number of cards (1-for-1, 2-for-2, etc.)\n6. No turns - it's a free-for-all\n7. Players try to collect four-of-a-kind in their hand\n8. When a player gets four-of-a-kind, they give their secret signal to their partner\n9. The partner calls 'Kemps!' to score a point\n10. If 'Kemps' is correct, the team scores\n11. If 'Kemps' is wrong (false alarm), the team loses a point\n12. Opponents can call 'Stop Kemps' or 'Counter-Kemps' if they think someone is signaling\n13. If a 'Stop Kemps' is correct, the calling team scores; if wrong, they lose a point",
    objective: "Be the first team to score a predetermined number of points (usually 5) by successfully calling 'Kemps' when your partner has four-of-a-kind, or by calling 'Stop Kemps' when an opponent is about to call.",
    gameplay: "1. Partners secretly agree on a signal (gesture, word, or movement) to indicate they have four-of-a-kind\n2. Each player receives 4 cards\n3. Four cards are placed face-up in the center\n4. When play begins, players simultaneously exchange cards with the center\n5. Players can swap any number of cards (1-for-1, 2-for-2, etc.)\n6. No turns - it's a free-for-all\n7. Players try to collect four-of-a-kind in their hand\n8. When a player gets four-of-a-kind, they give their secret signal to their partner\n9. The partner calls 'Kemps!' to score a point\n10. If 'Kemps' is correct, the team scores\n11. If 'Kemps' is wrong (false alarm), the team loses a point\n12. Opponents can call 'Stop Kemps' or 'Counter-Kemps' if they think someone is signaling\n13. If a 'Stop Kemps' is correct, the calling team scores; if wrong, they lose a point",
    keyRules: [
      'Partners must agree on a secret signal before play',
      'Signals can be gestures, sounds, or movements - but not words with meaning',
      'Players must maintain exactly 4 cards in hand',
      'The center must always have exactly 4 cards',
      'Card swapping is simultaneous - no turns',
      "First to touch a center card gets it if there's a dispute",
      "'Kemps' must be called by the partner, not the player with four-of-a-kind",
      "'Stop Kemps' can be called at any time",
    ],
